On Tue, 09 Dec 2003 07:54:07 -0800, Eric Wright wrote:

> Can someone give a brief overview on the chances for successfully
> discovering a trapped door/chest?  I've just lost 2 straight rogues on
> DLVL 1 from a trapped chest.  Each had a 18 DEX and searched for traps
> 4-5 times without success.

#untrap, not search [s], looks for traps on chests. If you're using the
number pad to move, you can use the keyboard shortcut [u]. 

If, otoh, this is what you were doing, then I'd call it a really bad case
of luck. Ont other thing: using skeleton keys reduces the chance of a trap
going off, as opposed to lock picks. If you've got the strength, carry the
chest and have patience until you have a key or more hit points. 



